  "notes": [
    "MaxRow lives on the HOST COLUMN, not the table Model — {\"Type\":\"Model\",\"AllowImport\":false,\"MaxRow\":2}. This is Kissflow's NATIVE row cap; no SDK/event enforcement needed. Do not confuse it with a MAX_LENGTH/MIN_LENGTH Criteria+Condition (FieldValidation-owned, a totally different Criteria usage keyed off a child FIELD, not the table) — that shape is out of scope here.",
    "Child columns are Start=0/End=0 always — the 6-unit row grid does not apply inside a table.",
    "PROVEN LIVE (2026-08-05): wiring the host Row into a Section's Column::Row PUTs 200, publishes 200, verifies on the wire — and still renders an EMPTY section. The host Row must be its own entry in the parent Model::Row, never inside a Section's Column::Row.",
    "New field type seen only as a table child in the wild: StarRating (also usable top-level, see field_star_rating.json)."
  ]
}
